      ],
      "text": "Introduction",
      "font": "SegoeUI",
      "size": 32.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.37223052978516,
        183.6797332763672,
        148.8199462890625,
        201.94973754882812
      ],
      "text": "Background",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 14.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        208.6555938720703,
        527.4156494140625,
        223.0985870361328
      ],
      "text": "Tuberculosis infection (TBI) is defined as a state of persistent immune response to stimulation by",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        220.57960510253906,
        524.3997192382812,
        236.29859924316406
      ],
      "text": "M. tuberculosis  (1) antigens with no evidence of clinically manifest TB disease  . As there is no “gold",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        235.0557403564453,
        527.3920288085938,
        249.4987335205078
      ],
      "text": "standard” test for TBI, the global burden is not known with certainty; however, about one fourth of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        246.9796905517578,
        527.4608764648438,
        262.6986999511719
      ],
      "text": "M. tuberculosis (2,3) the world’s population is estimated to have been infected with  . The vast majority",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.998350143432617,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        261.4556884765625,
        527.5787353515625,
        275.8987121582031
      ],
      "text": "of people with TBI have no signs or symptoms of TB disease and are not infectious, although they are",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.991045951843262,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        274.65570068359375,
        527.3793334960938,
        289.0987243652344
      ],
      "text": "at risk of developing TB disease and becoming infectious. Several studies have shown that, in recent",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        287.855712890625,
        527.4411010742188,
        302.2987365722656
      ],
      "text": "decades, an average 5–10% of people who are infected will develop TB disease over the course of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        299.77972412109375,
        527.46630859375,
        315.4987487792969
      ],
      "text": "(4,5) their lives, usually within the first 5 years after initial infection . The risk for TB disease after infection",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.963189125061035,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        312.97967529296875,
        527.4299926757812,
        328.6986999511719
      ],
      "text": "(1) depends on several factors, the most important being immunological status  . At the second United",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.986541748046875,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        327.4557189941406,
        527.3980102539062,
        341.89874267578125
      ],
      "text": "Nations high-level meeting on TB in 2023, Member States committed themselves to providing TPT",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        339.37969970703125,
        329.8852844238281,
        355.0987548828125
      ],
      "text": "(6) . to at least 45 million people between 2024 and 2027",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        361.0836181640625,
        527.4215698242188,
        376.8026428222656
      ],
      "text": "(7–9) TPT is a critical component of the WHO End TB Strategy and of other work to eliminate TB  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        374.2835998535156,
        527.4334106445312,
        390.00262451171875
      ],
      "text": "(1) The efficacy of currently available TPT regimens ranges from 60% to 90%  . The potential benefit",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        388.7596130371094,
        527.4301147460938,
        403.20263671875
      ],
      "text": "of treatment should, however, be carefully balanced against the risk of drug-related adverse events.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        401.9596252441406,
        527.4447631835938,
        416.40264892578125
      ],
      "text": "Mass, population-wide testing and treatment of TBI are not feasible at present because the tests are",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        415.1596374511719,
        527.4083251953125,
        429.6026611328125
      ],
      "text": "imperfect, there is a risk of serious, potentially fatal adverse drug reactions, and the cost would be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        428.3596496582031,
        527.4226684570312,
        442.80267333984375
      ],
      "text": "high, thus providing unclear benefit for populations at lower risk. The benefits of TPT are more likely",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        441.5596618652344,
        527.440673828125,
        456.002685546875
      ],
      "text": "to outweigh harm in infected individuals in population groups in whom the risk for progression to TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        454.7596130371094,
        527.5492553710938,
        469.20263671875
      ],
      "text": "disease substantially exceeds that of the general population. In people exposed to MDR/RR-TB, which",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.977978706359863,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        467.9595947265625,
        527.4196166992188,
        482.4026184082031
      ],
      "text": "is more difficult to treat than drug-susceptible TB, provision of suitable TPT may be more justifiable.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        481.15960693359375,
        527.3441772460938,
        495.6026306152344
      ],
      "text": "Programmatic management of TPT (PMTPT) involves a comprehensive package of interventions:",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        494.359619140625,
        527.4335327148438,
        508.8026428222656
      ],
      "text": "identifying and testing those individuals who should be tested, delivering effective, safe treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        507.55963134765625,
        527.4496459960938,
        522.0026245117188
      ],
      "text": "in such a way that the majority of those who start a treatment regimen will complete it with no or",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        520.7596435546875,
        527.3827514648438,
        535.20263671875
      ],
      "text": "minimal risk of adverse events, and monitoring and evaluation. PMTPT fits within a larger framework",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        533.9595947265625,
        527.4736328125,
        548.402587890625
      ],
      "text": "of preventive actions envisaged in pillars 1 and 2 of the End TB Strategy, from screening for TB disease,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.965295791625977,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        547.1596069335938,
        527.400390625,
        561.6026000976562
      ],
      "text": "infection control, prevention and care of HIV and other co-morbidities and health risks, access to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        560.359619140625,
        355.43896484375,
        574.8026123046875
      ],
      "text": "universal health care, social protection and poverty alleviation.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.37223052978516,
        585.2261962890625,
        132.19357299804688,
        603.4961547851562
      ],
      "text": "Rationale",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 14.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        610.2020874023438,
        527.5242309570312,
        624.6450805664062
      ],
      "text": "WHO guidelines on TPT are premised on the probability that TBI will progress to TB disease in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        623.4022216796875,
        527.4278564453125,
        637.84521484375
      ],
      "text": "specific risk groups, on the underlying epidemiology and burden of TB and on the feasibility and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        636.6021728515625,
        527.4232788085938,
        651.045166015625
      ],
      "text": "the public health benefit of the intervention. WHO global policy is expected to provide the basis for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        649.8021850585938,
        527.4100952148438,
        664.2451782226562
      ],
      "text": "the development of national guidelines for PMTPT, adapted to local circumstances. These guidelines",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        663.0020751953125,
        527.5470581054688,
        677.445068359375
      ],
      "text": "envisage a massive extension of TPT, including to individuals exposed to MDR/RR-TB, whereas global",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.99069595336914,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        674.9260864257812,
        527.4138793945312,
        690.6450805664062
      ],
      "text": "(10) coverage of the intervention is still very low, even in priority target groups  . The 2020 edition of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        688.126220703125,
        527.3611450195312,
        703.84521484375
      ],
      "text": "WHO consolidated guidelines on tuberculosis: tuberculosis preventive treatment  the  was the first in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.988794326782227,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        702.6021728515625,
        527.5449829101562,
        717.045166015625
      ],
      "text": "modular series of consolidated guidelines on various aspects of TB care, accompanied by operational",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.985740661621094,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        715.8021850585938,
        527.4227294921875,
        730.2451782226562
      ],
      "text": "handbooks. These documents were published on the WHO TB Knowledge Sharing Platform in 2021,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        727.72607421875,
        527.4246215820312,
        743.445068359375
      ],
      "text": "(11) and a training module with the same content was released in 2022 . The 2024 edition of TPT",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        740.9260864257812,
        527.4669189453125,
        756.6450805664062
      ],
      "text": "(12) guidelines and the associated operational handbook   will replace the earlier versions on the WHO",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.986141204833984,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        755.4022216796875,
        218.4481964111328,
        769.84521484375
      ],
      "text": "TB Knowledge Sharing Platform.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        547.8607177734375,
        801.0170288085938,
        551.980712890625,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "1",
